A||N||3||Wildcat||The Conversion Project Begins!!!!||||10||
Z||000000||Wildcat||04-25-2001||03:18 AM||||Hi All,<BR>Well we picked up a 3.1 litre chevy transport motor early 90's vintage today.  This is being used as a rebuild project motor.  $200 cdn for the motor.  It was running good when pulled but high miles on it.  So, off to the rebuilders we go.  We played "Let's Make A Deal" with the rebuilder, $1500cdn cash for a completely assembled motor.  New pistons, cam, valves, timing set, rings, bearings etc.<BR>This will include 18 months, 30,000km warranty as well.  I measured everything I could think of and it sure looks like it will bolt right in.  Thanks to all who provided advice here!  Hope to have the car on the road in 3 weeks (when son has the last of funds to pay for rebuild) and will let you know how the upgrade goes.  Hopefully this is the last time I ever have to do an engine swap on a Fiero! Too hard on the knukles! LOL!<BR>Tim||||reg||10
Z||000001||Raydar||04-25-2001||10:09 AM||||Cool! Best of luck. <BR>AFAIK, the 3.1 minivan motor is a <I>direct</I> bolt-in. I've heard that the minivan has smaller valves, though. (PLEASE someone correct me if I'm wrong. I'm not sure about this.)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Your rebuilder may know. Have fun! <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||14
Z||000002||RiceCooker||04-25-2001||12:56 PM||||Congrats and good luck<P>Whereabouts is williams lake?||||reg||6
Z||000003||Wildcat||04-25-2001||01:20 PM||||Williams Lake is about 220 kms south of Prince George on hwy 97.  <P>BTW with the 3.1 engine I will be using the flywheel off the 2.8litre.  Do I have to knock the balancing weight off it?<BR>Thanks,<BR>Tim||||reg||1
